# supabase/schemas — declarative schema, the source of truth for the database.
#
# Phase 0 ships this directory with zero tables in it. The pipeline is the
# deliverable, not the schema.
#
# The only supported way to change the database:
#
#   1. Edit or add a .sql file in this directory.
#   2. `pnpm supabase db diff -f <name>` to generate a migration from the diff.
#   3. Open a PR. supabase-migrations.yml verifies that the migration applies
#      against an empty database AND that this directory produces no further
#      diff -- i.e. that you actually ran step 2.
#   4. Merge to main. The Supabase GitHub integration deploys it.
#
# Note there is no deploy workflow in .github/workflows; deploys are handled by
# the GitHub integration configured in the Supabase dashboard.
#
# Never write a migration by hand against the live database, and never use the
# Table Editor or SQL Editor on the remote project. The same applies to the
# Supabase MCP connection, which has write access and bypasses migrations
# exactly the way a dashboard click does. Any of those turn supabase-drift.yml
# red within a day, and break `db push` with a sync error even sooner.
